<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oliba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 971–1046</span> · Also known as Abbot Oliba, Oliba of Vic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oliba was a Catalan churchman, a son of the count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerdanya">Cerdanya</a>, who became abbot of Ripoll and Cuixà in 1008 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Vic in 1018. He rebuilt the church of Ripoll, made its library a leading centre of learning and promoted the Peace and Truce of God in Catalonia. He is regarded as one of the most influential figures of early Catalonia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oliba.jpg" alt="Oliba" width="320" height="580" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Catalan Art &amp;amp; Architecture Gallery (Josep Bracons) from Barcelona, Catalonia · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abad_Oliva_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
